        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(imessage): remove split-send coalescing config",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes #91243. Replaces #107182 with a clean branch based on current `main` after the old PR became noisy/conflicted.\n\nThe iMessage plugin still exposed OpenClaw-side split-send coalescing config even though current `imsg` owns Apple URL-preview coalescing before OpenClaw receives messages. That left stale config/default surface area and confused upgrade proof.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- Removes the retired `channels.imessage.coalesceSameSenderDms` config/default/schema surface and the iMessage-specific URL-preview bucket policy.\n- Keeps the generic inbound debounce merge helper for configured `messages.inbound` batching, with narrow caps and tests.\n- Adds iMessage doctor legacy rules so `openclaw doctor --fix` removes retired root/account keys.\n- Lets doctor repair plugin-owned legacy config before strict runtime reads, without masking unrelated malformed plugin config.\n- Refreshes generated config baseline and bundled channel metadata.\n\n## User Impact\n\nExisting users no longer need or see the retired iMessage coalescing knob. Users upgrading with stale `coalesceSameSenderDms` config get a doctor repair path instead of runtime fallback behavior. Malformed non-legacy plugin config still fails closed and can recover from last-known-good during doctor repair.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `pnpm docs:list`\n- `pnpm config:docs:gen`\n- `pnpm config:docs:check`\n- `node --import tsx scripts/generate-bundled-channel-config-metadata.ts --write`\n- `node --import tsx scripts/generate-bundled-channel-config-metadata.ts --check`\n- `git diff --check`\n- Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kxkj9pzf835gy3nfb5z5zqhh`: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/imessage/src/monitor/coalesce.test.ts extensions/imessage/src/monitor.last-route.test.ts extensions/imessage/src/doctor-contract-api.test.ts extensions/imessage/src/probe.test.ts extensions/imessage/src/status.test.ts src/config/config.legacy-config-detection.accepts-imessage-dmpolicy.test.ts src/commands/doctor-config-preflight.test.ts src/commands/doctor-config-flow.test.ts src/flows/doctor-health-contributions.test.ts src/flows/doctor-core-checks.test.ts src/commands/doctor-session-transcripts.test.ts src/commands/doctor-session-sqlite.test.ts` passed 4 Vitest shards. Run: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29442698399\n- Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kxkjtn6kamxhwds5qfecab5d`: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/commands/doctor-config-preflight.test.ts src/config/config.legacy-config-detection.accepts-imessage-dmpolicy.test.ts` passed 2 Vitest shards. Run: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29443317150\n- Autoreview: `.agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode branch --base origin/main` clean; no accepted/actionable findings.\n\nKnown gap: no new live macOS iMessage send proof was collected for this replacement branch; this PR removes OpenClaw-side split-send policy/config and relies on focused unit/doctor/config proof plus the `imsg >= 0.11.1` ownership boundary documented here.\n",
        "branch": "agent/imessage-coalescing-clean-91243",
